---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About - China Massage Guide" description="Li Wei, TCM Practitioner — evidence-based Chinese massage and TCM education. Learn about our mission, credentials, and commitment to research-backed content.">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">About China Massage Guide</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-stone mt-8 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground">Our Mission</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          China Massage Guide exists to bridge the gap between ancient Chinese therapeutic traditions and modern evidence-based understanding. We provide independent, research-backed educational content about Chinese massage (Tui Na), acupressure, and Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) — free from commercial influence or practitioner referrals.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Every claim on this site cites a peer-reviewed study. We do not accept advertising or sponsored content from massage clinics or product manufacturers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground">About the Author</h2>
        <div class="mt-3 rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground">Li Wei, TCM Practitioner</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted">Registered TCM Practitioner | Specializing in Tui Na and Acupressure</p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Li Wei is a licensed Traditional Chinese Medicine practitioner with over a decade of clinical experience in therapeutic bodywork. She holds a diploma in TCM from the Beijing University of Chinese Medicine and is registered with the Chinese Medicine Board.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Her practice focuses on evidence-informed Tui Na, combining classical meridian theory with contemporary musculoskeletal research. She has contributed to patient education initiatives aimed at making TCM accessible to English-speaking audiences.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Li Wei is committed to transparency: she does not receive referral fees from clinics or product manufacturers, and her clinical recommendations are guided solely by patient need and available evidence.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground">Our Editorial Standards</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
          <li>Every article is reviewed for clinical accuracy by qualified TCM practitioners</li>
          <li>All health claims cite peer-reviewed research with PubMed-indexed references</li>
          <li>We clearly distinguish between established evidence and traditional theory</li>
          <li>Content is updated at least annually to reflect current research</li>
          <li>We disclose any updates or corrections with modification dates</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          For corrections, questions, or content feedback: <a href="mailto:contact@chinamassageguide.com" class="text-accent underline">contact@chinamassageguide.com</a>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted">
          This site does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. Always consult a qualified healthcare provider for health concerns.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
